    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by three high-upside plays that clear the 75-point threshold. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (77.01) is our premier option, benefiting significantly from a +14% boost due to a favorable platoon matchup against Teng, coupled with the run-production potential of batting leadoff. **Yordan Alvarez** (76.23) remains a foundational start; his elite xwOBA of 0.419 provides a high floor against Rea, and he remains our most reliable source for HR and RBI despite a moderate matchup. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (75.84) grades out as an elite play today, as the combination of a generous 5.11 xERA from Sasaki and a +13% platoon efficiency boost makes him a must-start in the cleanup spot.\n\nThe most aggressive play on the board is **Trea Turner** (69.64). While the \"Wind In\" advisory at the stadium is a minor drag, his stolen base potential remains the engine of our roster strategy. The optimizer heavily favors **Trea Turner** due to a +4% efficiency boost stemming from the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which creates an ideal environment for him to exploit the basepaths. Conversely, **Casey Schmitt** (50.65) narrowly held onto his starting spot. While he benefits from the 3-hole protection, his projection is hampered by a significant -11% dynamic platoon penalty against the southpaw Hudson; he is a marginal start who is only included to maximize plate appearances in a game with favorable wind conditions pushing out.\n\nRegarding the bench, the decision-making process was straightforward due to external volatility. **Junior Caminero** was the most painful omission, but his status was settled by a confirmed rainout, rendering his score a non-factor. **Kazuma Okamoto** was the closest to a starting role, but his matchup against the dominant Skenes\u2014who carries an elite 2.96 xERA\u2014coupled with his absence from the confirmed lineup, necessitated a benching to preserve our game caps. With **Caleb Durbin**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Colt Keith**, **Zac Veen**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** all sidelined, we are relying on our core starters to capitalize on their specific platoon advantages to keep our 5x5 pace steady.",
